From: Baptiste Faisy <baptiste.faisy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] platform/posix: gate MAP_32BIT on a feature test instead of an OS blacklist

MAP_32BIT is a Linux-specific mmap(2) flag. The current guard excludes
__APPLE__ only, so any other non-Linux target that ends up defining
BUILD_TARGET_X86_64 fails to build with:

    error: 'MAP_32BIT' undeclared (first use in this function)

Observed while porting to QNX 8.0 (SDP 8.0, qcc 12.2.0, -Vgcc_ntox86_64):
QNX <sys/mman.h> does not define MAP_32BIT. The aarch64le variant was
unaffected because BUILD_TARGET_X86_64 is not set for that target.

Testing for the feature instead of blacklisting operating systems keeps the
optimisation where it exists and lets every other target build unchanged.

Verified: with this patch, posix_memmap.c compiles cleanly with qcc 12.2.0
for both nto x86_64 and nto aarch64le, and the Linux build is unaffected
(MAP_32BIT is defined there, so the branch is retained).

Applies to WAMR-2.4.5 (commit 25bd7eb63e828e4bd242cc9b38d260b4b31c6605).
Apply from the repository root:  git apply < this-file   (or patch -p1)
--- a/core/shared/platform/common/posix/posix_memmap.c
+++ b/core/shared/platform/common/posix/posix_memmap.c
@@ -83,7 +83,9 @@
         map_prot |= PROT_EXEC;
 
 #if defined(BUILD_TARGET_X86_64) || defined(BUILD_TARGET_AMD_64)
-#ifndef __APPLE__
+/* MAP_32BIT is a Linux-specific mmap flag: test for the feature rather than
+   blacklisting operating systems. */
+#if defined(MAP_32BIT)
     if (flags & MMAP_MAP_32BIT)
         map_flags |= MAP_32BIT;
 #endif
